meta {
  name: Replay the same Idempotency-Key
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/loans
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "bookId": "{{bookId}}",
    "userId": "{{userId}}",
    "loanDays": 14
  }
}

docs {
  201, with the same loan id as "Lend a copy" and "replayed": true added.

  Byte for byte the response the first call produced, plus that one flag. No second loan is
  created and availability does not move again - run Books > Read availability before and
  after to confirm.

  This is the request that demonstrates the requirement. It is identical to the one above
  in every respect, which is the point: same key, same body, so the API answers rather than
  executes.
}
